<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RM_Weather_SlimeRain (spec §2) — "organism-induced, brief intense
    flooding, fast-draining, POTABLE (the body waters itself)".

    🔑 POTABLE IS THE POINT AND IT IS A REAL FIELD, NOT FLAVOUR. rainRate > 0
    is what makes vanilla treat this as rain at all: it fills roofless water
    collection, extinguishes fires, washes rainWashes filth (including this
    mod's own smear), and counts for plant growth. The campaign's Ash'karr
    has an R-H1 rule that makes its rain non-potable; that rule is CAMPAIGN
    canon (§1, left behind) and this mod deliberately does not carry it.

    Brief and intense: durationRange is a third of vanilla Rain's and rainRate
    is well above it, so the map floods and drains inside a few hours.

    Favorability Neutral, not Bad, deliberately: WeatherDecider refuses any
    below-Neutral weather for the first 8 days after settling
    (RimWorld/WeatherDecider.cs:156) and this is the biome's signature — it
    must be seen in the first week.

    ART: vanilla rain overlays plus a green sky tint. SkyManager
    (Verse/SkyManager.cs:117) tints any SkyOverlay with no ForcedOverlayColor
    using curSky.colors.overlay, so the green below reaches the falling
    particles for free — the same trick Pyrelands' ash fall uses. A bespoke
    drip sheet is in §7's owed art bill.
  -->

  <WeatherDef>
    <defName>RM_Weather_SlimeRain</defName>
    <label>slime rain</label>
    <description>The body sweats itself back into the sky and then lets it go all at once. Warm, heavy, faintly green, and over within a few hours; it fills every barrel on the map and drains away almost as fast. It is water — the organism is watering itself, and it is not fussy about who drinks. It also washes the smear off everything, which is the only free favour it does anybody.</description>
    <durationRange>7000~22000</durationRange>
    <favorability>Neutral</favorability>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <perceivePriority>3</perceivePriority>
    <accuracyMultiplier>0.8</accuracyMultiplier>
    <moveSpeedMultiplier>0.9</moveSpeedMultiplier>
    <rainRate>1.5</rainRate>
    <snowRate>0</snowRate>
    <windSpeedFactor>0.9</windSpeedFactor>
    <ambientSounds>
      <li>Ambient_Rain</li>
    </ambientSounds>
    <overlayClasses>
      <li>WeatherOverlay_Rain</li>
      <li>WeatherOverlay_Fog</li>
    </overlayClasses>
    <!-- `saturation` must never be 0 or WeatherDef.ConfigErrors complains. -->
    <skyColorsDay>
      <sky>(0.60,0.70,0.55)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.92,0.92,0.92)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.46,0.62,0.40)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.75</saturation>
    </skyColorsDay>
    <skyColorsDusk>
      <sky>(0.52,0.58,0.44)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.92,0.92,0.92)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.40,0.54,0.36)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.70</saturation>
    </skyColorsDusk>
    <skyColorsNightEdge>
      <sky>(0.20,0.26,0.20)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.85,0.85,0.85)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.22,0.32,0.22)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.60</saturation>
    </skyColorsNightEdge>
    <skyColorsNightMid>
      <sky>(0.18,0.24,0.18)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.85,0.85,0.85)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.20,0.30,0.20)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.60</saturation>
    </skyColorsNightMid>
  </WeatherDef>

</Defs>
